# Citation File Format (CFF) 1.2.0
# https://citation-file-format.github.io/
#
# Thot Secure is developed by an unaffiliated group of contributors; there is no
# single corporate author, so attribution goes to the collective. If you cite a
# specific release, cite the version and the tag you actually ran.
#
# `date-released` is deliberately omitted rather than guessed: it is added in the
# same pull request that cuts the release tag, so that the value in this file
# always matches a real release.

cff-version: 1.2.0

message: "If you use Thot Secure in research, in a publication, or in a product, please cite it using this metadata."

title: "Thot Secure: a defensive multi-tenant SOAR and CSPM platform"

abstract: >-
  Thot Secure is an open source defensive security automation platform (SOAR) with
  continuous security posture management (CSPM) capabilities. It ingests
  normalized telemetry from collectors, detects suspicious behaviour with
  declarative YAML rules, scores risk, decides a response through
  policy-as-code, and applies reversible counter-measures that are recorded in a
  tamper-evident hash-chained audit log. It is multi-tenant by construction,
  safe by default (dry-run enabled, supervised autonomy, explicit approval gate)
  and contains no offensive capability: it collects from and acts only on
  infrastructure a tenant has explicitly declared as owned. The project is
  distributed under the Apache License 2.0.

type: software

authors:
  - name: "The Thot Secure Authors"
    website: "https://thotsecure.dev"
    alias: "thotsecure"

contact:
